      "writtenOn": "2026-09-10T22:19:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There was a crash, yes. See https://build.aomedia.org/jenkins/job/libaom__commit_trigger/81729/\n\nAI-based analysis (not sure it\u0027s fully correct):\n```\nDynamic resolution upscaling without forcing keyframes relies on AV1 reference frame scaling. While real-time mode (oxcf.mode \u003d\u003d REALTIME) supports reference frame scaling for inter-frame prediction, the multi-pass / lookahead pipeline used in non-realtime modes (AOM_USAGE_GOOD_QUALITY) does not perform reference frame scaling during first-pass motion analysis (firstpass_inter_prediction in av1/encoder/firstpass.c).\n\nWithout conditioning on REALTIME, upscaling without a keyframe in non-realtime modes causes firstpass_inter_prediction (and aom_variance16x16) to read beyond the boundaries of the previous lower-resolution source/reference buffer (unscaled_last_source / last_frame), causing an AddressSanitizer heap-buffer-overflow crash in tests like AV1/FrameSizeChangeTest.*.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "5c6be761_100bad46",
      "revId": "9c63b1aeaea49bd5f36efc13bf46b9f125f12bdd",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
